<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ninisina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ninisina was the Mesopotamian goddess of healing and the patron deity of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a>, 'Lady of Isin'. She was regarded as a physician who cured illness, and dogs were her sacred animals; excavations at her temple uncovered dog burials and figurines. She was later merged with the healing goddess Gula.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ninisina.jpg" alt="Ninisina" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_goddess_Gula,_known_as_The_Great_Physician._Wellcome_M0006293.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
